{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg1252\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 Aptos;}}{\colortbl;\red24\green39\blue53;\red83\green96\blue108;}\pard\qc\f0\fs36\b\cf1 AURORA Website Copy Review\b0\par\par \pard\qc\f0\fs24\cf2 Editable copy worksheet\par\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 This document gathers the website wording as it currently appears, organized by page. Rewrite the passages in your own voice. Keep scientific facts, safety notes, fictional-project disclaimers, and source credits accurate. Leave web addresses and proper names unchanged unless you have verified replacements.\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Shared site text\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Brand: AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Button: MENU\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Navigation: Overview | Mission | Spacecraft | Crew | Research | Community | Reference\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Skip: Skip to main content\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Footer: AURORA is a fictional project about Mars exploration, not a real mission or spacecraft program.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Overview\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: AURORA | A Fictional Crewed Mission to Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: AURORA is a fictional, educational concept for a crewed mission to Mars. Explore the mission, spacecraft, crew and the questions it hopes to answer.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A fictional Mars mission\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Four people. One planet. Hundreds of days from home.\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 What would it take to send a crew to Mars and bring them home? Follow AURORA from launch through the long trip and back.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Follow the mission\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Explore the spacecraft\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Top-down view of the inner solar system. The dashed line is a simplified, energy-saving path from Earth to Mars. Mars has to be somewhere else when the spacecraft leaves than where it will be on arrival. Orbits are drawn as circles and sizes of planets are not to scale.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Mars Space Exploration Requires Many Jobs\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Science, Engineering, Medicine, and Leadership all contribute to a successful space exploration and research mission\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Field notes\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Five things to know about the destination\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Figures from the European Space Agency\u8217?s Mars fact page. See the Reference page.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 One Mars day\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 24 h 37 min Called a \u8220?sol.\u8221? Close to an Earth day.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Surface gravity\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 3.7 m/s\u178? About 38% of what you feel on Earth.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Atmosphere\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 95% CO\u8322? Mostly carbon dioxide, so humans cannot breathe it.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Width\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 6,794 km Roughly half the width of Earth.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 One Mars year\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 687 days A little under two Earth years.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech, PIA 17948 \u8212? Martian landscape with rock rows and Mount Sharp (stereo). NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Choose a path\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Where would you like to start?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Mission\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Goals, a timeline from launch to return, and a planner where you set the length of the trip.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Spacecraft\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 An interactive diagram of the six systems that keep four people alive.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Crew\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Meet the four fictional crew members and the jobs they would do.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Research\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Questions about Mars and what we still need to learn.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Community\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Sample school projects and ideas for sharing Mars exploration with a classroom.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: Curiosity's view of rows of rocks and Mount Sharp on Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram title: Top-down map of the inner solar system with a simplified Earth-to-Mars path\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram description: The Sun sits at the center. Around it are the orbits of Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars. A dashed curve leaves Earth's orbit on the left, swings around the Sun, and meets Mars's orbit on the right, where Mars will be when the spacecraft arrives. A second, solid Mars shows where the planet is at launch.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Mission\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Mission | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: The goals, timeline and trip-length planner for AURORA-1, a fictional crewed mission to Mars.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Mission dossier\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 AURORA-1: the plan\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A fictional four-person expedition to Mars, built to show how a real mission would fit together.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Goals and limits\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What AURORA-1 sets out to do\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Land four people on Mars, let them work there, and bring them home safely.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Study Mars\u8217?s rocks and ice to learn whether the planet was ever habitable.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Test how people, machines and teamwork cope with long distance.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What this project does not cover\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 This is not an engineering design. There is no budget, launch date or tested hardware. The route and schedule are examples, not plans for a real mission.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Mission timeline\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 From launch pad to home\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 1 \u183? Before launch\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Prepare and wait for the window\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Earth and Mars line up well for a trip only about once every 26 months, so missions must launch in a short window.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 2 \u183? Outbound\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 The long way out\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 AURORA-1 can pick a faster or slower route. A NASA planning study described a fast trajectory of about 180 days.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 How crews stay healthy and motivated for months in microgravity is still being studied.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 3 \u183? Arrival\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Enter orbit and descend\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A lander separates and carries the crew down. Mars\u8217?s thin atmosphere gives only some braking, which makes heavy landings hard.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 4 \u183? Surface\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Work on Mars\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Crew collect samples, test equipment and check for water ice. Messages to and from Earth take many minutes, so the crew must decide many things themselves.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 5 \u183? Return\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Wait, launch, and fly home\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 The trip home also depends on where Earth and Mars are in their orbits, so crews may need to stay for a long time.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stage 6 \u183? After landing\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Recovery and review\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Doctors check the crew, and engineers study what worked, so the next mission can be safer.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech, PIA 14832 \u8212? Artist\u8217?s concept of Curiosity approaching Mars. This depicts a robotic mission, not AURORA. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Try it\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Trip-length planner\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Choose a route and a stay on Mars. The planner adds up how long the crew would be away from Earth.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Route (each way)\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Faster route: about 180 days. Matches the fast trajectory in a NASA planning study. Needs more fuel.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Slower route: about 260 days. A round number we chose to show the trade-off. Uses less fuel.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Fuel consumption\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Relative fuel use for each route; exact amounts depend on spacecraft design and mission details.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Faster route\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Slower route\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Time on Mars: 30 days\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 180\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 days outbound\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 30\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 days on Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 180\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 days return\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 390\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 days total\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 12.8\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 months total\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A middle-length stay balances research time against time away from Earth.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Limits: this model assumes the return takes as long as the outbound trip and ignores planet alignment, so it is a teaching tool, not a flight plan.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8592? Overview\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Spacecraft \u8594?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: Artist's concept of NASA's Curiosity spacecraft approaching Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Spacecraft\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Spacecraft | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: An interactive concept diagram of the AURORA spacecraft and its six main systems.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Technology\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Connected Systems, Distinct Roles.\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A Mars mission crew depends on launch, entry and exit, life support, communication, navigation, and return capabilities. This page represents the roles those systems support in the AURORA concept.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 The descriptions are fictional. They do not represent actual spacecraft designs.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech, PIA 14832 \u8212? Artist\u8217?s concept of Curiosity approaching Mars. This depicts a robotic mission, not the AURORA spacecraft shown below. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Spacecraft systems\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A rough sketch, not to scale or an engineering design.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 1 Descent lander\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 2 Crew habitat\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 3 Radiation shelter\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 4 Supply module\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 5 Propulsion stage\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 6 Solar arrays\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 1. Descent lander\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Carries the crew from orbit down to the surface.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Mars\u8217?s atmosphere is thin, so it slows a spacecraft less than Earth\u8217?s does, yet it still heats the vehicle during entry. Landing something large and heavy is one of the hardest unsolved parts of a crewed mission.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 2. Crew habitat\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Where four people live, eat, exercise and work on the way to Mars.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Long stays in weightlessness weaken muscles and bones, so daily exercise is a core part of the plan. This concept leaves out exact room sizes on purpose.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 3. Radiation shelter\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A small, shielded space where the crew can wait out solar storms.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Radiation outside Earth\u8217?s protective magnetic field is a major health concern for long trips. How much shielding is enough is still being researched.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 4. Supply module\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Stores food, spare parts and recycling equipment for the whole trip.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Everything launched from Earth is costly, so crews would recycle as much air and water as possible and carry spares for repairs they cannot order.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 5. Propulsion stage\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Pushes the spacecraft out of Earth orbit toward Mars.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Space agencies have studied several engine types. AURORA does not choose one, because that decision needs real engineering analysis.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 6. Solar arrays\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Collect sunlight to make electricity for equipment, lights and life support.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Mars is farther from the Sun than Earth is, so sunlight there is weaker. A real design would have to account for that, and for dust storms on the surface.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8592? Mission\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Crew \u8594?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: Artist's concept of NASA's Curiosity spacecraft approaching Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram title: AURORA spacecraft diagram\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram description: A side view of a long spacecraft with six numbered parts: lander at the front, crew habitat, radiation shelter, supply module, propulsion stage, and solar arrays above and below. The same information is in the list next to this diagram.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Crew\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Crew | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: Meet the four fictional crew members of AURORA-1 and the roles a real Mars crew would need.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Crew roster\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 The four who would go\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Real expeditions succeed because of the people as much as the machines. These crew members are fictional, and each one stands for a skill a Mars mission would need.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Meet the crew\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Person 1:\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Njeri Mwangi. Black Female Commander. Born in Nairobi, Kenya and immigrated to the United States to teach chemistry at Princeton University. Soon went to work on the Artemis Vl mission, then helped test multiple Mars environments and probes, to later get promoted to the Aurora space exploration program.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Person 2:\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Hiroto Yamazaki. Japanese Male Doctor and Scientist. Born in Hiroshima Japan, he studied sports medicine at the University of Tokyo, where he also learnt English. Eventually the Aurora space exploration program recruited him.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Person 3:\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Gonzales Lacasa. Mexican Pilot. He was Born in Mexico City, Mexico. When he turned 14, his parents immigrated to the United States for better job opportunities. He got very interested in his fathers passion about the stars and space, so he studied for years to later apply for the Massachusetts Institute of Technology and got accepted to later become a pilot for Aurora.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Person 4:\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Logan Smith. Flight Engineer. Logan was born in Burlington, Vermont. He had great interest in mechanics, and generally how things work, from a very young age. When he entered the portal for a flight mechanics camp through his middle school, he discovered his strengths and was off to the races.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech, PIA 17948 \u8212? A view of the Mars landscape from the Curiosity mission. This is a real NASA rover image, not a portrait of AURORA\u8217?s fictional crew. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Several Areas of Expertise is Required.\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A Mars team would need science, medicine, piloting, and engineering experience and practice to be a successful team under high pressure situations.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 These profiles are fictional and do not represent any astronauts or selected people\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8592? Spacecraft\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Research \u8594?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: Curiosity's view of rows of rocks and Mount Sharp on Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Research\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Research | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: Six open questions about Mars that a crewed mission like AURORA would help answer.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Research questions\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 What we still want to know\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Mars still has plenty of unanswered questions. Here are a few worth investigating.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech, PIA 17948 \u8212? Martian landscape with rock rows and Mount Sharp (stereo). NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Want More Information?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What equipment is needed for Mars exploration?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What tools would be necessary for surface operations, and what measurements would they provide?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What life-forms have been discovered on Mars?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What effect do these life forms have on the actual planet and atmosphere around it?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 How should Martian sites be managed?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 What practices and procedures could countries do to create safer experiences?\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Data Should Be Available For Review\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Clear reporting makes it easy to access data about mission strategy, cost, limitations, and results. Public findings and international cooperation are also careful considerations.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 AURORA is a fictional educational concept. It is not an agency, active mission, or launch schedule.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Research Beyond Earth Has Its Limits\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Work on science, life support, medicine, and materials may inform research on Earth. All though this does not translate into direct benefits.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Space Exploration involves dangerous risks and heavy costs. Future goals on exploration should be decided on science goals, public opinion, crew safety, and cost.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 See our sources\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8592? Crew\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Reference \u8594?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: Curiosity's view of rows of rocks and Mount Sharp on Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Community\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Community | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: Sample classroom projects and ideas for bringing Mars exploration to a school community.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Classroom and community\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Mars ideas start close to home.\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A school project could invite students to imagine what people might need to explore Mars, then share their ideas through drawings, models and questions.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 A sample community gallery\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 These are made-up example posts to show how a future school or community showcase could look. The artwork is illustrative, not submitted by real students.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Sample post \u183? Spacecraft sketch\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 A ship with room for a garden\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A sample caption: \u8220?I added a plant room so the crew can grow some of their food on the trip.\u8221?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Sample post \u183? School activity\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Space ideas on the lunch table\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A sample community display could collect drawings and questions from a classroom event without showing student faces.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Sample post \u183? Rover idea\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Big wheels for a bumpy world\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 A sample caption: \u8220?My rover has wide wheels so it can get over rocks and carry tools.\u8221?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 From the NASA archive\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 NASA/JPL-Caltech/MSSS, PIA 20602 \u8212? Curiosity self-portrait at the Okoruso drill hole. This NASA archive image is separate from the fictional sample posts above. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Things a class could try\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 How a school project could work\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Start small\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Ask a teacher whether one class would like to try a short drawing or design activity. Share a simple prompt, give students time to create, and invite them to write a sentence about their idea.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Make a classroom gallery\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Display the work at school first. If the school and families approve sharing it, choose a few pieces for a community post and explain what the students designed.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Keep students safe: Get school and parent or guardian permission before sharing student work. Leave out children's full names, faces, schedules and identifying details. These sample posts are fictional; no school event or partnership is being claimed.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Accessibility descriptions (keep descriptions factual and useful)\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Image description: NASA's Curiosity rover taking a self-portrait at the Okoruso drill hole on Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram title: Sample student-style spacecraft drawing\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram description: A playful hand-drawn spacecraft with round windows, fins and stars.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram title: Illustration of a school community gathering\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram description: A school building, trees and a table with colorful spacecraft drawings, with no people shown.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram title: Sample student-style Mars rover drawing\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Diagram description: A simple rover with large wheels, a camera mast and a red rocky landscape.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb240\sa140\f0\fs30\b\cf1 Reference\b0\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Browser title: Reference | AURORA\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Search description: Sources, image credits, copyright notes and project documents for the AURORA website.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Sources and credits\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb180\sa100\f0\fs25\b\cf1 Reference\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Where our facts came from, what is original to this project, and the required TSA documents.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Required documents\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Student Copyright Checklist (PDF)\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Work Log (PDF)\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Sources for facts\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Facts are written in our own words. No text was copied from these pages.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 esa.int/Our_Activities/Space_Science/Mars_Express/Facts_about_Mars\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Used for: length of a sol (24 h 37 min), surface gravity (3.711 m/s\u178?), atmosphere (95.32% carbon dioxide), diameter (6,794 km) and orbital period (687 Earth days). The \u8220?about 38% of Earth\u8217?s gravity\u8221? figure is our own calculation: 3.711 divided by 9.81.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 nssdc.gsfc.nasa.gov/planetary/mars/marslaun.html\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Used for: launch windows about every 26 months, and the fast trajectory of about 180 days described in NASA mission planning.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Statements without a listed source. General statements about radiation, weakened muscles and bones in weightlessness, thin Martian air during landing, weaker sunlight at Mars, planetary protection, and radio delay are widely known. The same goes for the relative orbit distances in the Overview drawing (about 0.4, 0.7, 1.0 and 1.5 times Earth\u8217?s distance from the Sun for Mercury, Venus, Earth and Mars) and the shape of the transfer path. They have not yet been tied to a specific source on this page. The team still needs to add a citation for each one.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 Images, fonts and media\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Item | Where used | Source and rights\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Solar system path illustration | Overview | Drawn in SVG code inside index.html . No outside image used.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Spacecraft diagram | Spacecraft | Drawn in SVG code inside spacecraft.html . A concept drawing, not a real design.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Crew icons | Crew | Simple SVG circles with initials. No photos of real people.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Fonts | All pages | Fonts already installed on the viewer\u8217?s device. No font files are downloaded.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Martian Landscape With Rock Rows and Mount Sharp (Stereo), PIA 17948 | Overview, Crew, Research | NASA/JPL-Caltech. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Curiosity Approaching Mars, Artist\u8217?s Concept, PIA 14832 | Mission, Spacecraft | NASA/JPL-Caltech. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Curiosity Self-Portrait at Okoruso Drill Hole, PIA 20602 | Community | NASA/JPL-Caltech/MSSS. NASA image record .\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Audio and video | None | None used.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Archive images load directly from NASA\u8217?s image servers and require an internet connection. Captions identify the image credit and link to each NASA record.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\keepn\sb120\sa80\f0\fs22\b\cf1 How the site is built\b0\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 The site uses plain HTML, CSS and JavaScript. It uses no framework, no template and no theme, and it loads no outside libraries. NASA archive images load directly from NASA\u8217?s image servers; all other files are local. It collects no personal information.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 AURORA is a fictional concept for education. It is not endorsed by NASA, ESA or any other agency.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Team to complete before submission: confirm who wrote and made each part of the site, and add any outside help or tools the team used, as your advisor and the TSA rules require. Then delete this box. This statement was not written by the team and must not be left as is.\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 \u8592? Research\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par \pard\sa100\f0\fs21\cf1 Back to Overview \u8594?\par \pard\sa120\f0\fs18\i\cf2 Rewrite:\i0\cf1\par }